# Podium — environment variable reference
#
# This file lists every variable the backend needs.
# Copy it: cp .env.example .env
# Then fill in the real values. .env is in .gitignore and must NEVER be committed.
#
# Where each value comes from:
#   SUPABASE_URL          Project Settings → API → Project URL
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY     Project Settings → API → anon / publishable key
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY  Project Settings → API → service_role key  ← KEEP SECRET
#
# Note: For the Slido-style live rating tool, no Cloudflare R2 bucket or file uploads are required.

# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The ANON key is safe in the browser and in GitHub Actions (read-only via RLS).
# The SERVICE key bypasses every RLS policy — treat it like a root password.
# NEVER commit the SERVICE key to GitHub or expose it to client-side code.
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_YOUR-ANON-KEY
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=YOUR-SERVICE-ROLE-KEY-NEVER-COMMIT-THIS
